<stack-static>
    <statement><p><p>Simplify <m>{5 - 5\sin^2 x}</m> as far as possible.</p><div><fillin characters="18" name="ans1"/>  </div></p></statement>
    <solution><p><p>Look for <m>1 - \sin^2 x</m>, <m>1 - \cos^2 x</m> or <m>\sin^2 x + \cos^2 x</m>, perhaps after taking out a common factor, and replace it using <m>\sin^2 x + \cos^2 x = 1</m>.</p><p><me>{5 - 5\sin^2 x} = {5(1 - \sin^2 x) = 5\cos^2 x}</me></p></p></solution>
    <answer><p><m>5 \cos ^2\left(x\right)</m></p></answer>
</stack-static>